  "summary": "An oil-injected rotary screw compressor uses two meshing helical rotors. Gas fills the spaces between the lobes at the inlet end; as the rotors turn the pocket is sealed, carried along and made smaller until it opens to the discharge port. Injected oil seals, cools and lubricates; it is then separated from the air in the separator vessel and returned.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive-displacement compressor (rotary)",
    "type": "Twin-screw, oil-injected, single stage, direct drive"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "rotors": "Male 4 lobes / female 6 flutes",
    "capacity_control": "Inlet (suction-throttle) valve; VFD on many units",
    "separator": "Two-stage separation"
  },
